<title>HONG KONG: Shenzhen offers reward for info on VCD pirates.</title>
<headline>Shenzhen offers reward for info on VCD pirates.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's southern city of Shenzhen has offered a reward of 300,000 yuan for information on the location of illegal video compact disk (VCD) factories, the Shenzhen Special Zone Daily said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the government was determined to stop production of all illegal digital media in the city bordering Hong Kong and would guarantee the anonymity of informants.</p>
<p>Shenzhen is one of the main production centres in China of pirated VCD disks, CD-ROMS and music CDs, produced without approval from the copyright holders.</p>
</text>
